---
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from "../consts";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title={SITE_TITLE}
  description={SITE_DESCRIPTION}
  className="flex min-h-svh max-w-sm flex-col justify-center"
>
  <main class="space-y-4">
    <p>Hi! I'm Héctor.</p>
    <p>
      I'm a software engineer from Spain, passionate about building backend
      systems that run quietly and unnoticed in the background (that means they
      work).
    </p>
    <p>
      At <a href="https://emailmeter.com">Email Meter</a>, I handle vast amounts
      of real-time email data daily using Python, BigQuery, Dataflow, and AI for
      automated categorization.
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm also building <a href="https://www.reportative.com">Reportative</a>,
      which turns data from software and industrial devices into dashboards.
      Right now that means insulation monitoring: small Linux nodes read Bender
      insulation monitors on ships, plants and substations over Modbus, keep
      the history on site and ship it to a cloud where crews and shore offices
      see which board has a fault and what to do about it. Edge boxes,
      Tailscale, Kubernetes and ClickHouse, often without a reliable link to
      the outside world.
    </p>
    <p>
      At home I run a small server, automate the house with Home Assistant and
      keep a talking ESP32 on the desk. Some of it leaks out as side
      projects: <a href="https://md.hache.xyz">MarkShare</a>, a message relay
      for AI agents, and <a href="/blog/tailnet-acl-map">Tailnet ACL Map</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      I also love analog photography — feel free to explore my work in <a
        href="/gallery">/gallery</a
      >.
    </p>
    <p>🙋🏻‍♂️ 🇪🇸 ❤️ 🛠️ 🐍 ⚡ 📷</p>
  </main>
</Layout>
